6su9|n|To look down upon from a place that is over or above; to look over or view from a higher position; to rise above, so as to command a view of; as, to overlook a valley from a hill. ; Hence: To supervise; to watch over; sometimes, to observe secretly; as, to overlook a gang of laborers; to overlook one who is writing a letter. ; To inspect; to examine; to look over carefully or repeatedly. ; To look upon with an evil eye; to bewitch by looking upon; to fascinate. ; To look over and beyond (anything) without seeing it; to miss or omit in looking; hence, to refrain from bestowing notice or attention upon; to neglect; to pass over without censure or punishment; to excuse.	a:9qb1,39,3;8rmj,30,6;13pe,21,3;5uad,19,7;7ni3,18,14;9jei,18,1;3wx1,13,4;2lgi,12,9;36dg,0,4~7ni3,18,14;2lgi,12,9;5uad,19,7;8rmj,30,6;36dg,0,4;3wx1,13,4;13pe,21,3;9qb1,39,3;9jei,18,1	v:3duw,5,1~3duw,5,1	n:9qb1,43,4~9qb1,43,4	N:8ur1,10,93;5vdj,5,1;9qh2,4,6;fk7,3,19~8ur1,10,93;fk7,3,19;9qh2,4,6;5vdj,5,1
